1
00:00:06,114 --> 00:00:08,270
Hello, I'm Sangsoo Jeong.

2
00:00:08,271 --> 00:00:19,150
This chapter, before actually drawing a character concept art, let's briefly plan the design, talk about how to gather references, then proceed to the sketch.

3
00:00:19,369 --> 00:00:23,070
We need to decide what to draw before we draw.

4
00:00:23,930 --> 00:00:27,911
If it's company work or an outsourced job, you'd receive a document.

5
00:00:28,035 --> 00:00:38,580
Sometimes there's a detailed setting and story that'd remind you of a character from a grand novel, and other times they just toss you a few simple keyword words.

6
00:00:38,581 --> 00:00:47,341
Even preparing a game key art portfolio and simply deciding which character to draw can be considered part of character planning.

7
00:00:47,865 --> 00:00:53,460
If you're vaguely wondering what to draw, this process will help.

8
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:56,500
What's contained in a character planning document?

9
00:00:56,501 --> 00:00:59,380
Let me imagine a very simple document.

10
00:00:59,381 --> 00:01:02,781
Usually, we assume drawing a character concept key art.

11
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:08,510
Since this class only deals with humans, let's assume drawing a human.

12
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:10,590
You'd be divided into male and female.

13
00:01:10,591 --> 00:01:13,911
And the age group would be written, and the occupation would be written.

14
00:01:14,189 --> 00:01:16,430
And the era would be written.

15
00:01:16,431 --> 00:01:21,870
What era they lived in, what class they were, how they were living.

16
00:01:21,871 --> 00:01:22,871
Really simple, right?

17
00:01:23,074 --> 00:01:26,430
Surprisingly, sometimes you don't even get a document like this.

18
00:01:26,431 --> 00:01:29,790
With a document like this, you get lost as to what on earth to draw.

19
00:01:29,791 --> 00:01:34,350
So we need to expand this short planning.

20
00:01:34,351 --> 00:01:36,270
Let me see how to go about it.

21
00:01:40,704 --> 00:01:46,860
When I worked at a company, I usually received brief instructions before work.

22
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:53,260
For example, this picture was drawn on the instruction to draw a wild warrior character with a sense of weight.

23
00:01:53,474 --> 00:02:01,020
And this picture was drawn on the instruction to draw a filler with the keyword of a medieval nun, contrasting with the warrior.

24
00:02:01,021 --> 00:02:06,220
Both of these works were drawn when I was a twenty-six year old, three-year veteran, still a novice.

25
00:02:06,221 --> 00:02:09,419
I remember going through a lot of trial and error, working clumsily.

26
00:02:10,094 --> 00:02:13,130
I'm going to use that as an example.

27
00:02:13,131 --> 00:02:15,370
It's not a planning document, it's a sentence.

28
00:02:15,371 --> 00:02:19,610
I had my own ideas, changing the planning sentence of this picture.

29
00:02:19,611 --> 00:02:27,130
Since the motif is a nun, religious coloring shows through, but using a real religion is sensitive, so that won't work.

30
00:02:27,131 --> 00:02:29,770
Since it's a nun concept, let me draw it all black.

31
00:02:29,771 --> 00:02:32,410
It's a filler, so it'll be holding a staff.

32
00:02:32,411 --> 00:02:38,570
Thinking of religious items here, I thought of intricately crafted accessories or a staff, and so on.

33
00:02:39,470 --> 00:02:48,400
Since I drew it with only fragmented ideas, without considering that I was drawing a game character, I remember making a huge number of corrections as I drew.

34
00:02:48,401 --> 00:02:55,840
There are various elements to consider when drawing, but since this work, I've been picking out the silhouette.

35
00:02:56,514 --> 00:02:58,000
Why is that?

36
00:02:58,001 --> 00:03:06,080
While working as usual, there was something the producer requested importantly, and that was the variance between characters.

37
00:03:06,081 --> 00:03:07,081
Another thing was.

38
00:03:07,230 --> 00:03:11,600
That it should be clearly visible when the characters are scaled down small in the game.

39
00:03:12,564 --> 00:03:21,200
So since the warrior character was overall dark, I changed the healer character, which was also overall black, to white.

40
00:03:21,815 --> 00:03:25,440
And to make it visible within the game, it wears a cape.

41
00:03:26,785 --> 00:03:31,420
In game concept art, the contrast between characters is extremely important.

42
00:03:31,421 --> 00:03:33,100
Many of you play mobile games, right?

43
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:41,340
Because characters are crammed into a small screen, for distinction, the variance between jobs needs to be strongly felt.

44
00:03:41,341 --> 00:03:43,420
And it needs to be visible.

45
00:03:43,421 --> 00:03:52,220
Among the elements that can clearly distinguish the individuality of characters within a small screen are silhouette, value, and hue.

46
00:03:52,221 --> 00:03:55,621
Among these, the one that catches the eye the most is the silhouette.

47
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,680
Simply put, you need an effective big mass.

48
00:03:59,681 --> 00:04:09,360
Because of that, when I work on character design now, I put the character's variance, that is, the silhouette focused on big masses, as the top priority.

49
00:04:09,361 --> 00:04:14,000
I said you have to start big and finish fine.

50
00:04:14,001 --> 00:04:18,480
A silhouette set in a big outline sparks a variety of inspirations.

51
00:04:18,481 --> 00:04:22,240
That's why I do simplified sketches focused on the silhouette.

52
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:24,560
I'm not talking about the silhouette of a human body, or anything like that.

53
00:04:24,715 --> 00:04:25,860
Let me give an example.

54
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:31,940
This warrior character shows overall a massive quality that goes beyond the category of human.

55
00:04:31,941 --> 00:04:38,301
That worked effectively in the game too, allowing it to appear as a sturdy tank-type warrior character.

56
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:45,940
This healer character was drawn with a glamorous body overall, but honestly, at this level it doesn't show effectively in the game.

57
00:04:45,941 --> 00:04:49,700
So I added a cape to create volume.

58
00:04:49,701 --> 00:04:57,201
For this ranged dealer character, which has a relatively slim and normal body type, where did the silhouette come from?

59
00:04:57,590 --> 00:05:02,120
First, I equipped thick protective gear on the legs to reinforce the silhouette.

60
00:05:02,121 --> 00:05:04,040
But that wasn't enough.

61
00:05:04,041 --> 00:05:07,960
I was able to bring out the mass with a huge gatling gun.

62
00:05:07,961 --> 00:05:10,520
Is it enough to just add mass mindlessly?

63
00:05:10,521 --> 00:05:13,080
How should you add mass?

64
00:05:13,210 --> 00:05:17,800
Just as contrast between characters is important, contrast within a character is important too.

65
00:05:17,801 --> 00:05:21,360
My colleagues and I would call it concentrate and release.

66
00:05:21,750 --> 00:05:25,160
It's a good phrase to keep in mind when designing.

67
00:05:25,161 --> 00:05:30,120
For details too, concentrate where you should concentrate, and naturally release the rest.

68
00:05:30,121 --> 00:05:36,040
Likewise, for the silhouette, concentrate where you should, and release the rest.

69
00:05:36,041 --> 00:05:40,280
Shall we look at an example of concentrating and releasing in the silhouette?

70
00:05:40,281 --> 00:05:45,320
The warrior character has a body where a relatively massive upper body stands out.

71
00:05:45,321 --> 00:05:50,760
Because of that, the lower body got a silhouette only enough to naturally support that upper body.

72
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:53,950
The filler is the same.

73
00:05:54,110 --> 00:05:58,430
Since the cape takes care of the mass, I made the body fitted.

74
00:05:59,670 --> 00:06:04,520
The ranged dealer character also has the weapon taking care of the mass, so the body.

75
00:06:17,610 --> 00:06:20,860
The body could be relatively fitted.

76
00:06:21,425 --> 00:06:25,900
It's good to do this kind of variance from the planning stage.

77
00:06:29,469 --> 00:06:33,440
Next, the thing to think about is keywords.

78
00:06:33,441 --> 00:06:38,560
If I briefly organize the necessary contents of a planning document, it comes together like this.

79
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:49,600
Gender, age, class, era, value, hue, silhouette, body type, what to concentrate on, and keywords.

80
00:06:49,601 --> 00:06:56,681
For personal work, it'd be fun to add a brief background story or the character's personality.

81
00:06:57,520 --> 00:07:04,480
And the work instruction for this healer concept art can be organized like this.

82
00:07:04,481 --> 00:07:06,560
It was an instruction to draw a woman.

83
00:07:06,561 --> 00:07:09,200
And I set the age arbitrarily.

84
00:07:09,201 --> 00:07:12,320
Because it was an instruction to draw a healer.

85
00:07:12,321 --> 00:07:15,120
And it was a game with a medieval fantasy setting.

86
00:07:15,121 --> 00:07:17,280
It had the keyword of a nun.

87
00:07:17,281 --> 00:07:20,400
How can you fill in the remaining blanks?

88
00:07:20,401 --> 00:07:28,000
Usually, when you receive a planning document at a company, or get a verbal design request, they often give you settings from which you can infer the keyword.

89
00:07:28,705 --> 00:07:38,940
For example, like this picture, draw a healer with a nun concept, or put armor on a rose concept, and so on.

90
00:07:38,941 --> 00:07:41,820
Sometimes they give even more detailed settings.

91
00:07:41,821 --> 00:07:51,221
Like, in the beginning there were a god race and a demon race, and so on and so on. We have to use this keyword and branch out in various ways to design.

92
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:53,340
It's called drawing a mind map.

93
00:07:53,341 --> 00:07:57,180
Taking various words derived from the keyword as motifs.

94
00:07:57,395 --> 00:08:02,300
If you design that way, the design will be more consistent and convincing.

95
00:08:02,380 --> 00:08:04,700
You don't need to over-branch.

96
00:08:04,701 --> 00:08:14,860
Just as when we draw pictures or design, we establish a big frame then do detailed work, a big keyword and a few elements to support it are enough.

97
00:08:14,861 --> 00:08:18,700
Let me draw a mind map and establish the direction of the design.

98
00:08:18,701 --> 00:08:22,620
Freely write down related words, like spreading branches.

99
00:08:22,621 --> 00:08:25,100
Sometimes you form the design in your head.

100
00:08:25,555 --> 00:08:30,060
Or search the keyword on Google or Pinterest to get inspiration.

101
00:08:31,315 --> 00:08:33,820
The simpler the keywords, the better.

102
00:08:33,821 --> 00:08:36,220
I pursue simple designs.

103
00:08:36,221 --> 00:08:40,021
If the keywords are simple, the design is simple too.

104
00:08:40,670 --> 00:08:51,520
For example, this healer picture started with the keyword nun, and through a mind map a few supporting keywords were drawn out, and working with those allowed the design to take concrete form.

105
00:08:51,521 --> 00:08:54,240
Let me add these keywords to the planning too.

106
00:08:54,241 --> 00:08:57,600
This blue part is the planning added through the mind map.

107
00:08:57,710 --> 00:08:59,200
Nothing special, right?

108
00:08:59,201 --> 00:09:00,160
That's good.

109
00:09:00,161 --> 00:09:02,240
The design can become simpler.

110
00:09:02,241 --> 00:09:09,280
Like this, by drawing out keywords through a mind map and going into work, the design becomes more organized and you can reach a quicker conclusion.

111
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:11,620
It's also easier to find references.

112
00:09:11,621 --> 00:09:16,260
By varying the supporting keywords, you can also pull out various options.

113
00:09:16,261 --> 00:09:22,020
With this method, in later chapters, we'll plan the game concept art options.

114
00:09:22,021 --> 00:09:28,660
This time, I want to draw a character with a futuristic design, based on a healer style that was popular among my drawings.

115
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:33,060
Like this healer character, it'll likely be a character wearing a cape or coat.

116
00:09:33,061 --> 00:09:36,740
I want to do a clean design without any disorder.

117
00:09:36,741 --> 00:09:38,740
First, I'll draw a woman.

118
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:40,800
The reason is simple.

119
00:09:40,801 --> 00:09:51,840
Because more than half of consumers prefer female characters, and more than half of my classmates probably prefer watching a female character being drawn.

120
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:56,000
I say this many times, but we have to remember we're doing commercial art.

121
00:09:56,001 --> 00:09:59,520
For age, likewise, I'll draw a young woman.

122
00:09:59,521 --> 00:10:01,360
Around twenty to thirtyish.

123
00:10:01,361 --> 00:10:04,880
Because it's what consumers prefer, and it's less boring when it's refreshing.

124
00:10:04,881 --> 00:10:06,880
For occupation, I'll go with the magic class.

125
00:10:07,595 --> 00:10:09,220
This is my taste.

126
00:10:09,221 --> 00:10:12,980
When I play games, I mainly play magic-class characters.

127
00:10:12,981 --> 00:10:15,780
Especially, I prefer games with big, beautiful meteors.

128
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:20,740
For the era, let me go with a futuristic fantasy setting.

129
00:10:21,490 --> 00:10:26,180
I want to try an era I haven't drawn much, and colors I haven't used much.

130
00:10:26,181 --> 00:10:34,660
So for the use and hue, since it's a bright futuristic setting, I'll base it on a blue tone, per my own judgment.

131
00:10:34,661 --> 00:10:36,020
For the silhouette, likewise.

132
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:39,860
I plan to bring it out with a cape or coat.

133
00:10:39,861 --> 00:10:45,300
For the keyword, as I said, a clean and simple design.

134
00:10:45,301 --> 00:10:52,580
For the supporting keywords, as a result of going through a mind map, we set them to polygons, transparency, and light.

135
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:55,620
Let's start working with this planning.

136
00:10:55,865 --> 00:11:06,100
This way, by drawing up a brief planning and going into the work, the references to find are specified, quick envisioning is possible, and you can draw the picture systematically.

137
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:13,520
Especially the silhouette and hue keywords will be the key points of the design.

138
00:11:14,885 --> 00:11:21,120
This time, we had a time to make our own brief planning for a character concept.

139
00:11:21,121 --> 00:11:27,721
Next time, let's talk about how to gather and use references based on the planning.
